  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FTF Bangladesh Agricultural Infrastructure Development Activity (BAIDA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  The FTF Bangladesh Agricultural Infrastructure Development activity improves rural infrastructure in southern Bangladesh, especially rural roads, markets, collection centers, and drainage systems. The activity coordinates with other FTF activities to identify high-impact rural infrastructure projects that reduce travel time for farmers bringing their goods to market, improve the sanitation and safety of rural markets, and enhance the conditions of collection centers to reduce food waste. With FY 2024 funds, the activity will improve rural market roads, drainage systems, market centers and collection hubs to boost agricultural productivity, increase production, and strengthen food security. The activity works with local institutions to ensure the long-term sustainable maintenance of completed infrastructure projects, including local governments and market management committees. This activity supports the Global Food Security Strategy and the State-USAID Joint Strategic Plan goals two and three. Funding for the activity contributes to Global Food Security (GFS) ($2,850,000),Gender Equality and Women Empowerment Secondary ($600k) and Partnership for Global Infrastructure and Investment (PGI) ($2,600,000) earmarks and key issues.</narrative>
  </description>
